$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{(\ln(x))^3}{\ln(4x)}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[(\ln(x))^3\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[\ln(4x)]}\qquad\gray{\text{l’Hôpital’s rule}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{3(\ln(x))^2\cdot\dfrac{1}{x}}{\dfrac{4}{4x}}
\\\\
&=\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}3(\ln(x))^2
\\\\
&=\infty
\end{align}$

Note that we were only able to use l’Hôpital’s rule because the limit $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to\infty}\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[(\ln(x))^3\right]}{\dfrac{d}{dx}[\ln(4x)]}$ can actually be determined.
